{"name": "Core Chk'tu", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Chk'tu are tall, bipedal, insectoid vertebrates with sharp chitin-covered features, their exoskeleton covering their bodies like armor.  Most chk'tu feature chitin formations across their heads like helmets.  From spikes to horns to arches, these serve as hardened sensory antennae, and help regulate temperatures in their exoskeletal bodies.  Beneath these formations are two pairs of bead-like eyes and a set of vertically-split mandibles.  Their extra set of eyes grant them greater depth perception while fluttering, but their bead-like composition means that their four eyes are generally just as effective as a human's two.  Their mandibles hide both a tongue and internal chitin teeth that allows them to chew, drink, and, with practice, speak non-insectoid languages.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Chk'tu feature two to four arms, most of which are tipped with thin, four-fingered hands.  Along the backs of most chk'tu are a set of four wings between 3ft to 5ft in length that, when inactive, lay low like a cape behind them.  These wings give them limited fluttering or flight when vibrated, and are unhindered by rain and water when doing so thanks to their surprisingly soft, water-resistant exoskeleton.  Chk'tu have long, thin, digitigrade legs capped with four-pronged talon-like grippers at their base.  At the base of their torsos is a thin, tail-like abdomen that runs about 2ft long.  Generally, this \"tail\" is stiff and has a spiked appearance, and is primarily used for balance when jumping or fluttering.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Chk'tu come in a range of different colors, and rarely deviate heavily from the colors of their hive.  However, chk'tu that break ties with their birth hive often paint or stain their chitin to show individuality.  Chk'tu exoskeletons often feature a heavy solid coloring with contrasting accents or markings across their bodies.  Most chk'tu feature color palettes of blacks, purple-blues, greens, oranges, and browns, with eyes of black, green, red, or blue.  While other natural colors and color mixes exist, they tend to be much less common.  Chk'tu have viscous semi-clear blood that changes hue based on diet.  This usually ends up with semi-clear blood between dark green, pink, and yellow from diets primarily of vegetables, meat, or fruit.  The deeper the blood color, the less diversified the diet.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Chk'tu gather around royal chk'tu and create hives; massive singular complexes with winding pathways and numerous rooms meant for both housing and protection.  With few exceptions, chk'tu culture is utilitarian in nature.  Most hives being led by the long-living royal chk'tu means that the naturally short-lived are often given a static role to play, dedicating their life to their birth job.  Perhaps naturally, about 1 in 10 chk'tu abscond to find a new hive, to start their own, or to find some alternative form of living.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Chk'tu can appear very detached from the world at first, but many are passionate about their work, and quick to learn from their mistakes.  Other races consider their mental flexibility to be a necessity due to the chk'tu's short lifespan, while others point out that this simply serves to help chk'tu spread and create new hives faster than any other major race.  However, this is also why so many chk'tu abscond from hives, as their passionate nature means that a typical chk'tu is proud and curious, if defensive and unprepared, for what they will find in taking their true first steps alone from their hive.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Chk'tu Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Constitution increases by 1.</li><li><b>Lifespan: </b>Chk'tu reach maturity at around 1 year old, and live about 5 to 10 years on average.</li><li><b>Size: </b>Medium; Chk'tu stand between 5 to 7 feet tall and weigh between 100 to 200 pounds.</li><li><b>Speed: </b>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><b>Languages: </b>You can speak, read, and write Common and Chitter.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "M3S4OQLNOGHX7W5U", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Elf", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Elves are beings of lithe builds and swift action.  Moving faster than most of their counterparts in other races, elves tend to be quite dexterous and have an innate connection to the Fey that imparts minor magical properties unto them.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Elf Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Dexterity increases by 2.</li><li><b>Lifespan: </b>Elves actually reach physical maturity about the same time that humans do.  However, elves also live to be upwards of 700 years old, and thus have a different approach as to what truly makes you an adult.  Incidentally, most elves do not culturally have acceptance as adults until around 100 years of age, as they are judged by experience and knowledge, not years lived.</li><li><b>Size: </b>Medium; Elves are similar to humans, but are slightly smaller in stature.  They range from being a bit below 5 feet to just over 6 feet tall, and generally weigh within the range of 90 to 145 pounds.</li><li><b>Speed: </b>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in the Wisdom (Perception) skill.</li><li><b>Languages: </b>You can speak, read, and write Common, Elven, and one language of your choice.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EKY72M95PVXII7DV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Huagin", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Aquatic</p><p>Huagin are bipedal, aquatic, fish-like beings with scales ranging from skin-like smooth to fish-like sharp. They have long, thick tails attached to strong forms that have either two or four arms on them. Their heads are fish-like, often connected to thick, angled necks. These necks house their gills just under their dorsal fins, which are mostly concentrated on their head. These, with their webbed hands and feet, help them move through water at impressive speeds.</p><p>Huagin heads can vary in shape and type, sometimes with whiskers, sometimes with sharp teeth or large lips, sometimes more humanoid, sometimes with thick scales, sometimes with smooth. However, they all remain fairly uniform and recognizable. Their scales are monochromatic greens in the range of seafoam and teal, with fins ranging from greens to oranges and yellows. Their eyes have similar orange and yellow ranges with slightly vertical pupils. A common eye color for huagin are black eyes with black pupils, appearing as if dark orbs. These huagin are often jokingly called &ldquo;de huagin,&rdquo; a play on &ldquo;sea <em>de</em>vil,&rdquo; by other huagin, and is mainly said as a joke or compliment rather than an insult.</p><p>Huagin forms are humanoid, allowing them easy transition to and from land nations and cultures, but have a constant need for water to keep themselves from drying out. When remaining in water, their forms are capable, but are often slower than other fish in the sea. Their real strength, however, comes in their, well, strength. Facing a huagin in combat is asking for an onslaught of weapons and attacks big and small. Even those without extra arms are scarily capable at moving past defences, whether to kill or incapacitate.</p><p>Pair this natural capability in combat with the huagin culture&rsquo;s military organization and you may begin to understand why ancient civilizations dubbed them &ldquo;sea devils.&rdquo; This, however, also earned them a new title of &ldquo;sea angels&rdquo; from their supporters, who always felt they had someone watching over them while crossing the seas. Both of these perceptions come primarily because huagin are a wide-spanning culture that can be found in any part of the sea, with many allied huagin groups connected in a massive web of undersea territory. Allied flags were spread far and wide, and enemies never made it more than a few feet off the bow. Thus is the diplomatic power of a people that holds the majority of the world geometry.</p><p>Huagin have a long history of warlike tendencies, often viewing strength as the most important elements in life. It is for this reason that saba huagin often rise to the top of huagin society, with their extra size and arms often winning them one-on-one combat, at least on paper. In truth, many sa huagin, and even ba huagin have risen the ranks. There is no such thing as nepotism in huagin culture, as any who try it can only do so by backing their words up with actions. As a result, no matter who leads, the leader of a huagin society is something to be feared, both from their strong positioning and from the power they must personally wield to hold such a position.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Huagin Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Strength and Presence both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Huagin generally live around 30-40 years, and reach maturity at 4 or 5.</li><li><strong>Size: </strong>Medium; Huagin vary in height and size, but are generally quite tall, with the medium-sized ones typically being between 6-7 feet tall and weighing around 160-230lbs.</li><li><strong>Speed: </strong>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Swim Speed:</strong> You have a natural swim speed of 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Aquan.</li><li><strong>Amphibious: </strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.QEK74P09HWCNR1L5]{Amphibious}</li><li><strong>Aquatic Vocals:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.THVUXV1MHZ3DTIUJ]{Aquatic Vocals}</li><li><strong>Thirsty:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.9NXIJII89SBNXXMI]{Thirsty}</li><li><strong>Desalination Filter:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K9CRWETJD2UH9I7N]{Desalination Filter}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "R61VHJ537V5NM7G0", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Human", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Humans are bipedal, partially-haired mammals.  Each human\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s skin generally falls within a range of deep brown to light pale or peach, with different hues affecting this range.  Similarly, human hair has a wide range of browns, blacks, whites, reds, pale yellows, and anything between.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Generally, humans are broadly skilled and versatile creatures.  Their amount is numerous, and their styles are moreso.  They make homes in almost any climate, rely on tools to complete any task that they cannot, and have a wide range of cultural, political, and religious beliefs.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Human Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Pick three <i>different</i> Attributes, you increase each of these by 1.</li><li><b>Lifespan: </b>Humans reach adulthood in their late teens and live less than a century.</li><li><b>Size: </b>Medium; Humans are various when it comes to height and build.  Human height in feet can be anywhere from the low 5s to the high 6s on average, and their weight ranges from below 100 lb. to 200 lb. or more.</li><li><b>Speed: </b>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><b>Languages: </b>You can speak, read, and write Common and one extra language of your choice.  Humans can, and do, live across many different lands and with many different peoples, and often learn the languages of those they live or work with, no matter the obscurity or difficulty.  Humans often spice up their own speech patterns with words from a multitude of languages as well, especially languages they know. </li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6CJ7HA3IA7H2NW7O", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Kobold", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Kobolds are small reptilian creatures that walk and move like a humanoid but bear resemblance to the mighty dragons. These small creatures are very community based and are devoted to the betterment of their race and tribes as a whole. Every kobold has a place, a job to do, and they enjoy filling that role.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;They are rumored to be distantly related to dragons, and have been known to serve the mighty creatures in exchange for protection; because, while there is strength in numbers, there are still many things out there that are stronger. Thus, they look for those that will protect them from such beasts.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;While kobolds tend to stick together, it is not too uncommon to find them out adventuring, as their curiosity is only matched by their devotion to their race.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Kobolds have scale colors that match the color of their dragon ancestry, spanning both the chromatic and metallic spectrum. In this regard, kobolds of matching scale colors tend to live in tribes together, though it is not unheard of to have more than one scale color among a tribe. Eye colors are normally either amber, red, or violet.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;It should also be noted that kobold naming conventions are generally not those of the other races. Kobolds have only a first name, normally consisting of no more than one or two syllables, sometimes three if it is a name that consists of two hyphenated words, like the names of their racial branches. There are times where formally they will use their first name and their tribe name however, such as Zeke of Trostok.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Kobold Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Reptilian</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Dexterity increases by 2.</li><li><b>Lifespan: </b>Kobolds reach their age of maturity at 7 years old, and can live up to 125 years old.</li><li><b>Size: </b>Small; Kobolds stand between 2 to 3 feet tall and weigh between 25 to 35 pounds.</li><li><b>Speed: </b>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><b>Darkvision: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K2R4176S4B99TO6R]{Darkvision (30ft)}</li><li><b>Strength in Numbers:</b> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.XOU10R2EBHUGDPCQ]{Strength in Numbers}</li><li><b>Languages: </b>You can speak, read, and write Common and Draconic.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FKL170P16WQV8I25", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Insectoid</p><p>Lep&rsquo;ix are bipedal, insectoid vertebrates with a smooth, generally monochromatic exoskeleton. Their figure is crested by large multi-colored wings like those of a butterfly&rsquo;s or moth&rsquo;s. Shorter on average than humans and chk&rsquo;tu, their frame is generally lighter and more lithe, with tapered thin arms and legs that contain surprising strength. Insectoids that they are, lep&rsquo;ix also possess a pair of large, round, compound eyes, a mandibled set of mouthparts, and a crown of bent, fern-like antennae. Their eyes can be almost any color, particularly dark hues, vibrant reds, yellows, silvers, and greens. These often come with gradients and unique fresnels, and may have a sort of metallic or iridescence gleam to them. Especially when lighter, they may also appear to be polka dotted with black spots.</p><p>Lep&rsquo;ix wings are often vibrant, covered with highly detailed patterns made up of basic shapes. With the ability to manipulate their wing colors, some lep&rsquo;ix are capable of more dynamic patterns, such as parts partially moving or changing color. No two Lep&rsquo;ix wings are alike in shape or pattern, which makes a lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s wings their most defining feature, especially amongst non-insectoids. Lep&rsquo;ix wings are soft but flexible, and delicate yet durable. They are also self-mending&mdash;a lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s wings often tear during combat, but if not too bad, they&rsquo;re able to reform throughout the month. Lep&rsquo;ix wings are also capable of folding downward like a folding fan behind them. However, some lep&rsquo;ix are born without this muscle, leaving their wings inflexibly pointed out behind them without a tie to harmlessly wrap or fold.</p><p>Genetically, some lep&rsquo;ix can also grow a thick, fur-like mane around their neck or chest, trailing off along the head and shoulders. More rarely going as far as the wrists, up the wings, or to the waist. This &ldquo;fur&rdquo; is actually a set of thin chitin bristles, soft and velvety to the touch as an animal&rsquo;s fur can be. Against a lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s thin physique, this can give them a top-heavy look, especially when their wings are spread wide. While a genetic difference, this coat is mostly aesthetic and does not determine a lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s racial traits, as a human&rsquo;s beard wouldn&rsquo;t.</p><p>Upon reaching maturity, lep&rsquo;ix tend to form a connection to a mystical origin. When this happens, their magical powers grow and their wing patterns evolve into their final design, affected by the sphere of influence with which they are most closely tied. While the exact cause of a lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s individual connection to a magic source is shrouded in mystery, lep&rsquo;ix communities are usually blessed by just one origin. This has led to a theory that their wings or body absorb latent magics and evolve to match the energies most active in their environment. But why lep&rsquo;ix are so tuned to the magic in the air is another question entirely. Theories have long placed lep&rsquo;ix as being immigrants from planes far beyond our own, a theory often corroborated by lep&rsquo;ix themselves. However, histories of their origins are oft&rsquo; contested, even conflicting by implying multiple origins of equal validity.</p><p>Conjecture aside, meeting a lep&rsquo;ix is a different experience altogether. Lep&rsquo;ix cultures can be fairly different per magical influence, but a common strain is high-level sociality. Lep&rsquo;ix are oft&rsquo; expected to interact under a higher degree of scrutiny and with a higher level of pomp and tact, regardless of scenario or the speaker&rsquo;s education. And with the inclusion of their shifting wings and graceful motions, this gives them further layers of communication with those around them. Ever circumspect, an interaction with a lep&rsquo;ix about the weather can be just as active as a battle or playful as tag. As a result, Lep&rsquo;ix are often viewed as masters of their own presence, with grace and control that brings a certain energy to a room they&rsquo;re in. One lep&rsquo;ix may carry a seraphic grandeur, while another may be intimidating and gloomy, and another quick and sharp. What that presence is can vary, but one rarely fails to leave a strong impression on a room.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<h4>Core Lep&rsquo;ix Traits</h4><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Presence score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Delicate Wings:</strong> Your Constitution score decreases by 1. <br />If your branch race grants you a flying speed or a duplicate <em>Flutter Fall</em> ability, ignore this penalty.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Lep&rsquo;ix reach maturity around 5 years old and live to 50 or 60 years on average.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> Medium; Lep&rsquo;ix are generally between 4 to 5 feet tall (not counting their wings), and weigh between 70 to 140 pounds.</li><li><strong>Speed:</strong> Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Chitter.</li><li><strong>Compound Eyes:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.TW3Q20EW6IL08P3K]{Compound Eyes}</li><li><strong>Weak Build:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.9LRGBCE9H4Z9YXF9]{Weak Build}</li><li><strong>Flutter Fall:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.G7NRS6CYBK7GV2WW]{Flutter Fall}</li><li><strong>Captivating Patterns:</strong> Covered in tiny scales and hairs that are capable of shifting colors, your wings are a tapestry of mesmerizing patterns. You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.S19PI54SQR9C8R14]{Captivate} cantrip.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AWDQLRXTNDMKD2LO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Mecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p><em>&lsquo;How deceptive,'</em> it&rsquo;s been said, <em>&lsquo;that mecians appear like rats of our world but have minds from another.&rsquo;</em></p><p>Mecians are short and lithe creatures, with long faces, a long tail, and moveable ears. Their faces are tipped with whiskers under a pink or black nose, and a long-muzzled mouth with two buck teeth. Their eyes are either a solid opaque without iris or pupil, or have colored irises around white pupils. The opaque and iris colors pull from the same pool, primarily being black, pale, shades of red or pink, or a dark ruby, being black with a red reflective sheen. Less common colors include off-white (which usually comes with a slightly darker rim around the iris), yellow, pearlescent, and a dark citrine or topaz. Regardless of color, mecians are often described as having blank or emotionless eyes, not being the muscles with which most mecians emote. Mecians are covered head-to-toe in short, dense fur of varying shades of grays, tans, browns, and blacks. About half the time this comes in two-toned colorations, with the darker color typically covering either their head, their head and back, or their head, back, and arms. This second tone can be solid, come in spots, or have spots that group into larger, more solid groups. Mecian noses can also sometimes have darker colorations. Their hands, feet, tail, nose, and ears are typically a pink-tan color, and are more sensitive than the rest of their body. Their tails are long and tapered, as long as about half their standing height, and are fully articulate. Mexican tails are also dextrous enough to be usable as a third limb for simple tasks. Mecian genealogy has a higher mutation rate, with especially albinism, gigantism, and heterochromia being more common in mecians than most other races.</p><p>Mecians, when first met, tend to be underestimated. With a naturally lithe and diminutive appearance and blank stares, folks are likely to find mecians more awkward than harmful. However, what doesn&rsquo;t show on the surface is that mecians are impressively wired creatures. Their thoughts are quick and powerful, moving their body with a certain intensity and precision not unlike creatures half their size, and the minds of those twice that. At a young age, this can manifest as a twitchy or nervous nature, moving in precise bursts of energy followed by stillness. Although this behavior refines significantly with age&mdash;it&rsquo;s said you can tell a mecian&rsquo;s age by handing one a full goblet and watching the drink&rsquo;s ripples.</p><p>Blessed with unusual minds, their uncanny thoughts are naturally telepathic, but in a limited scope. Like an active radio, they are able to &lsquo;hear&rsquo; the crackling static of the minds around them.</p><p>They can even convey certain feelings through this mind field, if to a limited degree. Regardless, what they send and say is limited and garbled, but can act as a guide for others around them to understand them beyond what their faces convey. This ability is intensified when coming in contact with others. As if using their body as a conduit, they can create a sort of psionic closed circuit with another creature, making the sharing of thoughts and feelings more possible. It&rsquo;s not uncommon for mecians to hold their tails at certain angles to get better &lsquo;reception&rsquo; on the fragments of an emotion they&rsquo;re enjoying, or to privately converse with another by leaning together, linking tails or hands, or bumping into each other.</p><p>In a world of magic and multitudes, one might expect to see more mecians interspersed across the realms. Indeed, under normal circumstances they multiply like flies. However, mecians are a race deeply bonded with their own&mdash;their slightly psionic nature makes them fantastic at communication with each other, but their reliance on it makes communication with others more difficult. Mecians from purely mecian societies simply lack the experience needed to use more subtle facial and vocal expressions, coming off blunt and cold as a result. This isn&rsquo;t helped by the mecian&rsquo;s natural emotional fortitude that can cause them to come off as unfeeling. In short, mecian accents, mannerisms, and culture are all influenced by their telepathy. When able to convey feelings without words, words alone feel deficient&mdash;it&rsquo;s not their fault that others can&rsquo;t &lsquo;hear&rsquo; their true hearts. But to others, the difference between a caring and heartfelt mecian and a twisted and malicious one can be difficult to tell at a glance, too difficult. Unsurprisingly then that mecians tend to live with their own, and tend to stick together when traveling. Indeed, travelers have yet to disprove the saying: &lsquo;where there&rsquo;s one mecian, there&rsquo;s two.&rsquo;</p><p>That said, those mecians who have been forced to live without their kind tend to find new ways to feel connected to their new homes and neighbors. These mecians also tend to be more expressive, communicating and integrating well with their neighbors after overcoming an adjustment period.</p><p>Wherever they settle, mecians have great potential as technical laborers, scientists, and more. An individual&rsquo;s potential, however, is rarely achieved. Any society where mecians live tends to overflow with them through sheer duplicative force. As a result, mecians are often forced to choose between proving their worth over their brothers and sisters or standing with them. For the latter, mecians who stick together do so like glue, overcoming group failures and celebrating group victories&mdash;nothing is done alone. These mecian communes, referred to as &ldquo;pods,&rdquo; can be anything from transactional to gestalt in nature, and all members may even share the same name to reflect this. To choose to stand alone, however, can be especially difficult&mdash;any personal failures can seem mountainous to overcome without a pod at your side, and overcoming them may draw more malice from those around you. However, lone achievers do tend to crawl to the top of the pile, meaning lone mecians are often have the most to both gain and lose. In either lifestyle, mecians find a way to thrive in all societies worldwide.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Mecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity and Intelligence each increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Mecians tend to live to about 70 years, and are considered full adults at around 15-20.</li><li><strong>Size: </strong>Small; Mecians are on the taller side of small creatures. Their head-to-foot height is usually around 3-4 feet tall, and the length of their tails are just shorter than half of their standing height. In general, healthy mecians weigh between 35-80 lbs.</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Size:</strong> Medium; Occasionally, mecians are born extra tall, being at least a few feet taller than their brethren. These are genetic mutations unrelated to heredity and happens to somewhere between 1 in 100 and 1 in 1000 mecians&mdash;rare, but common enough to be recognized as a quirk of mecian genealogy.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li><strong>Speed: </strong>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Landspeak.</li><li><strong>Nimble Tail:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.0YU2TJMLJPZVTTPR]{Nimble Tail}</li><li><strong>Passive Reception:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.NG6ZJR57CL9WRGV9]{Passive Reception}</li><li><strong>Touch Telepathy:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.N6TTMSUFM57X8K16]{Touch Telepathy}</li><li><strong>Cold Mind:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.10AP60QZ8JQR8BT7]{Cold Mind}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6TD9YHW3QVCQGM74", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Minotaurs are bipedal beings reminiscent of humans, but with a head resembling a bull&rsquo;s, hooved feet (usually white, black, or a blend), and a full or partial covering of short, bovine fur. Minotaur fur generally comes in shades of brown, black, white, or a mixture of those colors. Generally a solid color, minotaurs are sometimes born with larger splotches of color or smaller sets of freckles. Skin colors can vary as much as humans, but feature a wider spectrum of reds and browns.</p><p>Regardless of sex, the head of a minotaur is adorned with a formidable pair of solid, bull-like horns, often built of stronger stuff than even their bones. In minotaur culture, it&rsquo;s said that the horns are the most important part of the body, and much can be gleaned from the handling of one&rsquo;s horns. Not to be overstated, minotaur culture puts much stock into preserving their horns. To many, it&rsquo;s their history worn bare, every scrape or nick has a story to tell, and plays a part in minotaur socializing and cultural pride.</p><p>Minotaur bodies tend to be built larger than humans, with the average minotaur sharing a height with some of the tallest and largest humans. Be it for muscle or fat, it&rsquo;s not uncommon for minotaurs to find other races scrawny or unhealthy looking in comparison.</p><p>Minotaur society is that of adaptability. Minotaurs are all born of the same stock, but grow rapidly in their adolescence, evolving to meet the challenges natural to their environment. It&rsquo;s said that minotaur strength meets their match in nature, and many minotaur groups choose to face that challenge head on.</p><p>The result of all this is one of the more formidablely resilient races, to such an extent some wonder if minotaurs may have been created through magical means. While not shared by all of their kind, to many minotaurs, it hardly matters. The truth is what&rsquo;s before them and what&rsquo;s in their reach. The future is unknown, but the present makes a past worth wearing with pride.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Strength and Constitution scores both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Minotaurs reach adulthood in their mid-teens and few live past 80 years of age.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> Medium; Minotaur height generally ranges from 5&frac12; to 7 feet tall, and their weight ranges from below 150 lb. to 275 lb. or more.</li><li><strong>Speed:</strong> Your base walking speed is 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Landspeak.</li><li><strong>Horns:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.8PHJHUPTCSNNWE71]{Horns}</li><li><strong>Bull Rush:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.FSYAETXYEA3YJSPS]{Bull Rush}</li><li><strong>Trailblazer:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K44RS5GZ07MOGUI1]{Trailblazer}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1E5LPEA0RDN5EZIX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p>Spelled &ldquo;Ya&gdot;ruda&rdquo; in Ave, yarhuda are lightweight, bipedal avians with crooked beaks, piercing eyes, and long, wing-like ears. A plume of large, soft, water-retardant feathers covers most of their upper body, draping partially over their shoulders and midsection like a natural poncho or cloak. Their torso is covered with much smaller feathers, with legs mostly bereft, causing some yarhuda to wear armor and clothing beneath their plumes for safety and comfort. These plumed feathers serve more than just to shield them from the elements. Yarhuda have surprising control over their feathers, able to angle or flare them at will by controlling the muscles around them. Depending on the yarhuda, some feathers can be quite rigid and or sharp, and can be angled or flared out for use in controlling their momentum.</p><p>The yarhuda&rsquo;s most striking ability, however, is their unusual method of flight. The thickest and largest feathers around their neck are attached to a special muscle that yarhuda can flex to make spin on its axis around its collarbone. Yarhuda put their arms down at their side and angle their spinning neck feathers to create lift, allowing them to fly. A yarhuda&rsquo;s control over their feathers remains impeccable, able to open, flatten, or curve their rotor feathers even during flight. Furthermore, their heads are topped with a small pair of wings sprouting from their head like ears. These can be rapidly flapped to control which way they&rsquo;re facing mid-flight and keep themselves from spiraling&mdash;a pair of natural second rotors. When combined with a lesser control over their arm and body feathers, yarhuda are able to move through the air with incredible ease.</p><p>Yarhuda usually have greyish skin with shades of blue or black, but their feathers have much more diversity. While typically falling into shades of dark blues, purples, and blacks, it&rsquo;s possible for yarhuda to have deep greens, cyans, and oranges or browns. Regardless, their feathers have a slight iridescent sheen to it, and usually flows together naturally, rather than having sharp patterns. Yarhuda beaks are crooked and intense, typically with calm grey, tan, or black colorations. However, some yarhuda branches are born with much brighter colors. Even for those without brighter beaks, a painted beak isn&rsquo;t uncommon for yarhuda as a show of style or affiliation.</p><p>In a similar way, a common aspect of yarhuda culture are masks, either over the head, beak, or both. These have cultural and stylistic significance, but originally came from a desire to buffer the intense wind in their face that that their method of flight causes. Dying feathers, especially bleaching them, is a relatively common phenomenon as well for similar reasons. Beyond this, leg wraps and pants are common amongst yarhuda to keep warm, with special light body armor used when combat is involved.</p><p>Yarhuda can be found all over, but are particularly prevalent in high altitude, high-perching environments. They tend to build homes in precarious locations, such as atop of trees or on cliffs, as they have little fear of falling in these situations and give them easy lift for takeoff. This preference has forced yarhuda engineering to be particularly adept to support such precarious setups.</p><p>Yarhuda are sometimes seen as wintry, with stoic faces and a strong exterior that often belie their more passionate nature. The wind is a gift, one that yarhuda never underestimate. Those who cannot fly may spend their time constructing wind-utilizing art or architecture. Some use their masterful feather control to make wind sculptures, temporary and complex shapes and air currents visible through fine colored dust. Yarhuda wind dancers use this to an entirely unique effect, pouring colored dust under their feathers, which they hold in place until the moment they choose to release it, allowing certain movements to be accented with vibrant winds.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity and Intelligence each increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Yarhuda reach maturity around 8 and tend to live up to age 60.</li><li><strong>Size: </strong>Medium; Yarhuda are tall avians with long legs and many feathers on their upper half. They tend to stand within a range of 5-6 feet tall, sometimes taller, with a typical weight range of 90-120lbs. Some branches range up to 200lbs.</li><li><strong>Speed: </strong>Your base ground speed is 25 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Ave.</li><li><strong>Helix Wings:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.KYSYXGJ0975JHGQV]{Helix Wings}</li><li><strong>High Altitude Adaption:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.SWQIHGVCC7ULP8LY]{High Altitude Adaption}</li><li><strong>Racial Trinket:</strong> You own a pair of goggles or a yarhuda flight mask. <br />Yarhuda masks and goggles are a common part of yarhuda culture, helping keep wind and dust out of their face during flight. These can vary in shape and design from simple leather googles, to long-nosed incense masks, to more flat-face masks.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EBEI44BIBBKA2PEF", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Core Zhier", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Zhier are quadrupedal, extremely long living, sapient beasts somewhere between a wolf and a large feline. They typically have short fur, long, tuft-tipped tails, agile bodies, and tough manes either around the neck or spine. Their fur color stretches from more naturalistic oranges and whites, to striking blues and greens, and is often accented by certain amounts of dyed fur. Their manes range from full-neck manes like a lion, to tracing the spine like a hyena, and in either instance, the manes can be soft and silky or rough or scraggled. Their wolf-like eyes on the other hand, are fully genetic, with yellow or gold, orange, hazel, light brown, light green, amber, and blue being most common.</p><p>As one of the few fully intelligent quadrupeds, Zhier often have a difficult time fitting into bipedal societies, but their resilience and mental flexibility makes adaptation easier than one might think. Despite their lack of hands, zhier mouths are incredibly well evolved to hold, manipulate, and wield objects. Zhier have impressively strong neck and jaw muscles that allow them to quickly pick up and wield weapons that most would struggle to use with one hand. In fact, many zhier prefer gripping a weapon in their teeth over biting and tearing that might chip their valuable teeth. Weapons can be sharpened and repaired, and bring versatility and range to the table that teeth alone cannot. The more hominid races are often bewildered by a zhier&rsquo;s intelligence, mistaking them for talking lions, wolves, tigers, etc. As versatile as they can be, zhier are considered an anomaly in the animal kingdom, and so outside influences, whether deities or strange magics have been suspected. Though asking a zhier will lead to the conclusion that it&rsquo;s their connection to nature that defines their shape, not the other way around.</p><p>To this point, all zhier are born with a deep, personal connection to an element of nature that is said to permeate them to their very core. This connection is both physical and spiritual, manifesting most obviously in a zhier&rsquo;s corresponding fur color. This element is most highly attuned, however, to the tip of their tail, which radiates with their element. In a pinch, zhier can swing their tail at creatures like a flail that bursts with elemental energy to injure their target. <br />A zhier&rsquo;s control over their spirit element grows with them over time, and the nurturing of this gift can be considered a spiritual experience in its own right; an act of self-improvement. Surprisingly, these elements are not genetic&mdash;Zhier of one element can give birth to a zhier of any other. Some say that the element is based on a zhier&rsquo;s personality, or that the personality is based on the element. Others relate it to seasons or weather or even energies in the air. No matter the case, the elemental attunement has a great effect on a zhier&rsquo;s life, determining what capabilities and roles it can undertake. Zhier mythology considers these elements a gift of nature, a call to action unique to each zhier. This can be taken further with the introduction of their sign.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Core Zhier Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity and Wisdom both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> Zhier live tremendously long lives, with some being known to live into the low thousands. Zhier reach a physical maturity sometime in their 30s-40s. However, their extended lifespan gives them a different perspective on mental maturity, with most zhier being considered adults between their 70s-90s.</li><li><strong>Size: </strong>Medium; Zhier are typically around 4 to 5 feet long and 2-2.5 feet high while on all fours, and can weigh between 120 to 200 lbs.</li><li><strong>Speed: </strong>Your base ground speed is 30 feet.</li><li><strong>Languages: </strong>You can speak, read, and write Common and Landspeak.</li><li><strong>Skill Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in the Wisdom (Instinct) skill.</li><li><strong>Inhuman:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.EQWTTLVYL3B2EALU]{Inhuman}</li><li><strong>Quadruped:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1TYQ7CP70PTQ1KLX]{Quadruped}</li><li><strong>Mouth Grip:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2AAUZETAFQSEKV9M]{Mouth Grip}</li><li><strong>Strong Jaw:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.AABF3VD0XLSXJW60]{Strong Jaw}</li><li><strong>Somatic Tail:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.US9E7VG69DJXD7WX]{Somatic Tail}</li><li><strong>Light Mount:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.T147SCK0L9JBNDJ4]{Light Mount}</li><li><strong>Howl:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.XRZMC82H6U0DER0Y]{Howl}</li><li><strong>Element Flail:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.3QPFSY40NDIM3XL9]{Element Flail}</li><li><strong>Spirit Resistance:</strong> You are resistant to the damage type associated with your Spirit Element.</li><li><strong>Spirit Element:</strong> All Zhier are born with a physical and spiritual connection to an element said to permeate them to their very core. A zhier&rsquo;s control over their spirit element grows with them over time, and the nurturing of this gift can be considered a spiritual experience in its own right; an act of self-improvement. <br />Surprisingly, these elements are not genetic&mdash;Zhier of one element can give birth to a zhier of any other. Some say that the element is based on a zhier&rsquo;s personality, or that the personality is based on the element. Others claim the weather in the last few weeks before a birth can determine its element. No matter the case, take one spirit element from the following table, alongside all associated racial traits.</li></ul><p><em>Spirit Element Table</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"min-width: 70px; margin: 0 5px;\"><p><strong>Spirit Element</strong></p></td><td style=\"min-width: 70px; margin: 0 5px;\"><p><strong>Fur Color</strong></p></td><td style=\"min-width: 70px; margin: 0 5px;\"><p><strong>Spirit Casting</strong></p></td><td style=\"min-width: 100px; margin: 0 5px;\"><p><strong>Flail Description</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Cold</p></td><td><p>Shades of white.</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.J5UHXN59MY3NP3VV]{Spirit Casting (Cold)}</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.O27T8DMCLZPKT1W3]{Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Cold)}</p></td><td><p>Your tail tip is covered with visible hoarfrost that freeze-burns the point of collision.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Fire</p></td><td><p>Shades of orange.</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.OCP4C1AL9OIF3NRK]{Spirit Casting (Fire)}</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.VFSHRL6BWD7HQMXQ]{Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Fire)}</p></td><td><p>Your tail tip has a small flame at its tip, searing the point of collision.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Lightning</p></td><td><p>Shades of blue.</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YNBPIYB4O41QRD6N]{Spirit Casting (Lightning)}</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.6HMQFQZ7A29OJEGP]{Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Lightning)}</p></td><td><p>The fur on your tail tip arcs with low-level electricity, jolting the point of collision.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Poison</p></td><td><p>Shades of green.</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.15AYWYZJLABDJ09Z]{Spirit Casting (Poison)}</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YJYHZV2J65GS21QS]{Spirit Casting Additional Trait (Poison)}</p></td><td><p>Your tail tip has small, poisonous quills that prick a target on contact.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RH9S24KDUC5SJJGL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
